  "question": {
    "text": "From a point $(\\mathrm{d}, 0)$ three normals are drawn to the parabola $\\mathrm{y}^{2}=\\mathrm{x}$ then"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{d}=\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{d}>\\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{d}     < \\frac{1}{2}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\quad \\mathrm{d}=\\frac{1}{3}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "We know for $\\mathrm{y}^{2}=4 \\mathrm{ax}$, if we draw a normal from $(\\mathrm{h}, 0)$ then, condition for three normal is $\\mathrm{h}>2 \\mathrm{a}$.\r\nNow, $y^{2}=x$\r\n$\\therefore \\quad d>\\frac{1}{2}$"
  }
}